2017-03-31   *  Vincent B Coen
		This section updated 31-03/2017.
		This code base includes not only the code for ACAS but
		also extras to support mysql and other rdbms systems.
		These directories / sub directories are not required for
		compiling the system but to support new code for rdbms
		modules/routines that are still in development.
		These directories include rdbms, rdbms-win 
		and experimental-stuff. << This may not be present >>

		To compile the system go into the ACAS Source directory,
		and run comp-all.sh having ensured that you have built the
                GNU Cobol compiler and run all tests (make all).

		This does 'assume' that you have the GNUCobol compiler
		v1.1 or later installed and tested. It is RECOMMENDED that
                you use v2.0.


		Manuals for all systems & sub systems are still in a state
		of rebuild/rewriting and should olny be taken as a general
		guide. Hopefully you can spot where the original manuals are
 		still present in each document. As coding AND testing
		continues these are being updated but I only have one pair 
		of hands :)

                All manuals including the source of very old one's are in
		ACAS-Manuals directory. 
		See the stock and irs ones for information on building the
		various systems and running them.

		Note that other than creating the system file via the menu
		option on all/most systems as option Z ACAS will create each
		when required. IRS is slightly different - Read the manual.

		Additional programming support is always welcome so get in
		touch at vbcoen at gmail.com or via the forum and let me know
 		how you can help.


